WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.208 --> 00:00:01.958
This is a syringe full of water.

00:00:01.958 --> 00:00:04.458
I've closed off this end 
so it can’t escape.

00:00:05.125 --> 00:00:07.208
And no matter how hard I push...

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:09.958
Nothing really happens.

00:00:10.916 --> 00:00:12.083
I can't compress it.

00:00:12.416 --> 00:00:15.625
Even if I put this inside 
an industrial hydraulic press...

00:00:15.708 --> 00:00:18.750
a machine that can push down 
with thousands of tons of force...

00:00:19.083 --> 00:00:22.041
the volume would only decrease by about 1%.

00:00:22.583 --> 00:00:24.666
But what if it was squeezed even harder?

00:00:24.708 --> 00:00:26.208
What if this water was subjected

00:00:26.208 --> 00:00:28.333
to the extreme pressures 
in the Earth's core?

00:00:29.041 --> 00:00:30.916
Or inside the Sun?

00:00:32.291 --> 00:00:33.500
What would happen to it?

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:36.750
The answer is something really bizarre.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:39.625
Something physicists are just starting 
to understand.

00:00:39.833 --> 00:00:41.750
In many ways, this is 
really a new field.

00:00:41.791 --> 00:00:44.291
We just don't fully know the rules yet.

00:00:44.541 --> 00:00:46.541
It's an entirely new regime of matter.

00:00:46.708 --> 00:00:50.000
To try and wrap our heads around 
these extreme pressures

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.416
and the way they warp physics 
as we know it.

00:00:52.916 --> 00:00:55.333
Let's go on a journey 
straight down.

00:01:06.625 --> 00:01:09.958
We'll start our trip up here on the surface 
at atmospheric pressure.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:12.791
How much pressure is that exactly?

00:01:12.791 --> 00:01:14.000
How does it compare to, say

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.291
the pressure of my phone 
on my palm?

00:01:16.833 --> 00:01:18.833
Well, the phone's weight, 
about two Newtons...

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.583
is spread out over about 
100 square centimeters.

00:01:21.666 --> 00:01:22.916
That's how pressure is measured:

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:24.958
A force distributed over an area.

00:01:25.666 --> 00:01:27.208
The pressure of the atmosphere

00:01:27.208 --> 00:01:29.333
the hundreds of miles of air above me...

00:01:29.583 --> 00:01:33.500
pulled down by Earth's gravity 
is 500 times stronger.

00:01:33.833 --> 00:01:36.291
That's like the pressure my phone 
would exert on my palm

00:01:36.291 --> 00:01:39.791
if Dwayne “The Rock” Johnson 
was balancing on top of it.

00:01:40.416 --> 00:01:42.333
But because the air is free 
to flow around...

00:01:42.541 --> 00:01:45.666
it's also pushing up The Rock 
with the same pressure.

00:01:46.041 --> 00:01:48.875
Every phone sized patch of my body 
is getting pressed

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:51.291
inward by the equivalent of 
The Rock's weight.

00:01:51.583 --> 00:01:54.083
Of course, all the structures 
and fluids within my body

00:01:54.083 --> 00:01:55.041
are pressing back

00:01:55.041 --> 00:01:57.833
and I'm so used to this equilibrium 
that I don't even notice.

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:00.083
Before we leave these familiar conditions

00:02:00.083 --> 00:02:02.125
I'm going to grab a few things to take with us.

00:02:02.458 --> 00:02:05.666
A gram of hydrogen, 
a gram of sodium...

00:02:06.666 --> 00:02:08.166
and a kilo of water.

00:02:08.875 --> 00:02:11.791
We know exactly how these substances 
behave on Earth’s surface.

00:02:12.208 --> 00:02:14.541
But what happens when 
we start to squeeze?

00:02:16.458 --> 00:02:18.541
Just ten meters of seawater adds

00:02:18.541 --> 00:02:20.541
another whole atmosphere 
worth of pressure.

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:23.458
27 floors down...

00:02:23.958 --> 00:02:26.125
we pass the unassisted diving record.

00:02:26.416 --> 00:02:27.375
And just a little deeper...

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.250
we hit ten atmospheres.

00:02:30.333 --> 00:02:32.541
Now we're going deeper than 
the deepest scuba dive.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:34.708
There's a blob of fish.

00:02:34.875 --> 00:02:36.958
They look like depressed jello 
on the surface

00:02:36.958 --> 00:02:39.291
but down here, the pressure 
keeps them trim.

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:43.333
One kilometer down, 
we reach 100 atmospheres.

00:02:43.666 --> 00:02:46.791
The kinds of pressures we got with that 
giant hydraulic press.

00:02:47.875 --> 00:02:49.791
Sperm whales can dive this deep...

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:53.541
and their hinged rib cages fold inward
so the bones won't snap.

00:02:54.416 --> 00:02:56.583
Here, the Titan submersible 
was crushed...

00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:00.833
and here is the destination 
they never reached.

00:03:00.833 --> 00:03:03.916
[My Heart Will Go On by Celine Dion
plays briefly]

00:03:04.833 --> 00:03:06.875
Somehow we're still passing fish.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:10.166
And now we've reached the bottom 
of the Mariana Trench...

00:03:10.416 --> 00:03:12.375
and 1000 atmospheres.

00:03:12.875 --> 00:03:15.500
We're now up to the pressure of a phone
with a herd of elephants

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:16.708
balanced on top.

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:19.250
Let's check in on the samples we brought.

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:20.833
Our balloon of hydrogen gas

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:23.000
has shrunk down to the size 
of a big marble.

00:03:23.333 --> 00:03:26.500
But both our solid sodium and liquid water 
haven't changed much.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:27.958
They're just barely compressed.

00:03:28.375 --> 00:03:29.583
Why is that?

00:03:29.583 --> 00:03:31.375
Well, the molecules of hydrogen

00:03:31.375 --> 00:03:32.708
had plenty of space between them.

00:03:32.708 --> 00:03:33.916
Room to shrink.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.666
But the sodium and water were 
already tightly packed.

00:03:37.041 --> 00:03:38.958
Even the pressure down here can't overcome

00:03:38.958 --> 00:03:41.875
the electrostatic repulsion 
between molecules.

00:03:41.875 --> 00:03:43.625
It's nowhere near strong enough.

00:03:44.125 --> 00:03:45.458
But let's keep going.

00:03:46.541 --> 00:03:48.750
Every meter of rock 
piles on the pressure

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:50.625
nearly three times faster 
than water.

00:03:50.916 --> 00:03:52.375
The temperature is rising, too.

00:03:52.791 --> 00:03:56.166
As we leave the crust, we hit 
10,000 atmospheres.

00:03:56.708 --> 00:03:59.750
In the mantle, temperatures shoot past 
a 1000 degrees Celsius

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:01.208
and some of the rock starts to melt.

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:03.875
This is where many diamonds form.

00:04:04.166 --> 00:04:06.791
Carbon is squeezed into a tight crystal.

00:04:07.416 --> 00:04:11.041
As we go deeper into 100,000 
atmospheres of pressure...

00:04:11.166 --> 00:04:14.833
the rock is compressed further,
forced back into its solid form.

00:04:15.833 --> 00:04:17.583
Our sodium, meanwhile, has melted...

00:04:17.875 --> 00:04:20.291
and our bubble of hydrogen 
is liquid too.

00:04:20.291 --> 00:04:22.458
Compressed into a little clear globule.

00:04:22.875 --> 00:04:24.208
The water is also changing.

00:04:24.458 --> 00:04:27.958
It's getting squashed so much, 
it's forced to become a solid.

00:04:28.375 --> 00:04:30.583
But not the hexagonal crystals 
we get on the surface.

00:04:30.958 --> 00:04:32.791
Instead, it's a tighter cubic lattice.

00:04:33.125 --> 00:04:36.166
Scientists have found 
this variation of ice, Ice-VII...

00:04:36.416 --> 00:04:38.125
trapped inside diamonds.

00:04:39.291 --> 00:04:40.958
As we get close to Earth's core

00:04:40.958 --> 00:04:43.375
we pass 1 million atmospheres.

00:04:43.708 --> 00:04:46.791
That's the equivalent of an oil tanker 
balanced on a phone.

00:04:48.375 --> 00:04:49.625
This is the threshold

00:04:49.625 --> 00:04:52.625
we're now leaving the world that 
physicists fully understand.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.625
This is where the external forces

00:04:55.625 --> 00:04:57.291
are about the same

00:04:57.291 --> 00:04:59.875
and starting to overwhelm 
the internal forces.

00:05:00.083 --> 00:05:02.541
The crushing pressure is starting 
to overcome

00:05:02.541 --> 00:05:05.791
the electromagnetic forces holding 
water molecules apart

00:05:05.791 --> 00:05:06.958
apart and maintaining their shape.

00:05:07.541 --> 00:05:10.583
The behavior that 
comes out of being

00:05:10.583 --> 00:05:14.333
in these extreme conditions 
is pretty bizarre.

00:05:14.333 --> 00:05:16.708
How do you study matter 
under conditions

00:05:16.708 --> 00:05:19.041
that normally only exist 
deep inside the earth?

00:05:19.291 --> 00:05:23.666
That was the point of creating the 
Center for Matter at Atomic Pressures.

00:05:23.666 --> 00:05:26.041
We're going to be doing all the 
fundamental physics

00:05:26.041 --> 00:05:27.416
to be able to understand matter

00:05:27.416 --> 00:05:29.583
under these really different 
kinds of conditions.

00:05:29.666 --> 00:05:32.166
CMAP is headquartered at 
the University of Rochester...

00:05:32.291 --> 00:05:35.500
and they've got a tool that helps them
create extreme pressures.

00:05:35.791 --> 00:05:39.750
The enormous Omega EP laser 
which fills this giant room.

00:05:41.166 --> 00:05:42.500
This is the facility's schedule.

00:05:42.625 --> 00:05:43.833
Scientists from around the world

00:05:43.833 --> 00:05:45.416
queue up for months 
just for a chance

00:05:45.416 --> 00:05:48.250
to blast a tiny sample of matter 
with a laser beam.

00:05:49.041 --> 00:05:50.666
And how do you feel in the run up to this?

00:05:51.208 --> 00:05:52.916
Unbelievably nervous.

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:55.958
You spent a year of planning 

00:05:55.958 --> 00:05:58.416
and crossing T's and dotting I’s...

00:05:58.583 --> 00:05:59.958
just to get to this point.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.083
The shot director gets on the intercom 
and he goes—

00:06:03.083 --> 00:06:03.500
Five...

00:06:04.083 --> 00:06:05.750
four, three...

00:06:06.291 --> 00:06:08.000
two, one.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.791
[silence]

00:06:09.791 --> 00:06:14.041
Shot 39607 
is now complete.

00:06:14.791 --> 00:06:15.791
That was it.

00:06:15.791 --> 00:06:18.375
During that split second, 
a million atmosphere pressures 

00:06:18.375 --> 00:06:20.375
were momentarily created in the next room...

00:06:20.791 --> 00:06:23.500
the same pressures that exist deep within Earth.

00:06:24.333 --> 00:06:26.125
How does a beam of light do that?

00:06:26.541 --> 00:06:27.625
Let's go through it again.

00:06:27.625 --> 00:06:29.000
Just way slower.

00:06:34.125 --> 00:06:37.208
The laser beam is born in these machines 
down in the basement...

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:39.500
and it's directed through a maze of lenses

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:41.750
and devices that shape 
and monitor it.

00:06:42.291 --> 00:06:44.041
Bouncing through these 
massive tubes...

00:06:44.166 --> 00:06:47.875
it's infused with more power until 
it's as wide as this opening:

00:06:47.875 --> 00:06:50.083
About 45 centimeters across.

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:52.375
Then it races towards the target chamber

00:06:52.375 --> 00:06:54.833
which is hidden behind this tangle 
of equipment.

00:06:56.250 --> 00:07:00.208
This is a visual representation 
of the target chamber.

00:07:00.375 --> 00:07:03.958
And the target is right at the center of it.

00:07:04.875 --> 00:07:07.708
Those are really, like a pinpoint...

00:07:07.791 --> 00:07:11.083
on the tip of a pen, 
just absurdly small.

00:07:11.333 --> 00:07:13.750
The target is a tiny, 
inedible sandwich

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:16.875
with a sample of whatever substance 
the researchers are interested in 

00:07:16.875 --> 00:07:17.500
in the middle.

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:20.500
The laser light is focused down 
to hit this first layer

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:23.875
which explodes into a 
superheated ionized gas.

00:07:24.166 --> 00:07:27.666
And that plasma blows off of 
the surface like a rocket.

00:07:27.666 --> 00:07:31.791
Ahat creates this buildup of pressure 
that forms a shockwave.

00:07:32.125 --> 00:07:35.333
And that shockwave really quickly travels
through the material.

00:07:35.541 --> 00:07:37.166
The last layer acts as a window

00:07:37.166 --> 00:07:39.291
allowing the passage of electromagnetic rays

00:07:39.291 --> 00:07:40.875
generated during the experiment.

00:07:41.416 --> 00:07:42.875
And then surrounding it

00:07:42.875 --> 00:07:46.416
you have these spaces 
to put different cameras

00:07:46.416 --> 00:07:47.750
and other tools that we use

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:50.125
to measure the various things 
that we're interested in.

00:07:50.166 --> 00:07:51.625
If you look through this porthole...

00:07:51.958 --> 00:07:55.041
you can see a couple of these sensors
getting moved into place.

00:07:56.583 --> 00:07:59.625
In 2017, researchers put a tiny bit of Ice-VII

00:07:59.625 --> 00:08:00.958
sandwiched between two diamonds...

00:08:01.166 --> 00:08:02.250
in the target chamber.

00:08:02.583 --> 00:08:04.041
As the shockwave passed through it...

00:08:04.333 --> 00:08:07.291
pressure in the ice spiked 
above 2 million atmospheres

00:08:07.291 --> 00:08:08.833
and its atoms rearranged.

00:08:09.083 --> 00:08:11.000
Oxygens formed a tight lattice...

00:08:11.208 --> 00:08:13.708
while hydrogens were free 
to diffuse through it.

00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:17.958
It was Ice-XVIII, four times denser 
than normal ice...

00:08:18.083 --> 00:08:20.708
and able to conduct electricity 
almost as well as a metal.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.541
For a few billionth of a second...

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:25.791
the laser had recreated conditions 
inside Earth.

00:08:26.666 --> 00:08:28.291
Speaking of, let's get back 
to our journey.

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:30.833
As our water starts 
to turn into Ice-XVIII...

00:08:31.166 --> 00:08:34.583
our glob of sodium is undergoing 
its own transformation.

00:08:34.875 --> 00:08:38.541
Under these pressures, scientists have seen
it turn transparent.

00:08:39.333 --> 00:08:40.791
Now, what could account for this?

00:08:40.916 --> 00:08:42.833
Well, metals like sodium are shiny

00:08:42.833 --> 00:08:45.458
because they have a bunch of 
free-flowing electrons

00:08:45.458 --> 00:08:48.041
that can absorb and then retransmit light

00:08:48.041 --> 00:08:49.750
which we see as a reflection.

00:08:49.875 --> 00:08:52.750
What happens when you apply pressure to it

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:56.000
is you're squeezing the electrons 
away from their atoms...

00:08:56.250 --> 00:08:58.333
and into these localized pockets.

00:08:58.375 --> 00:09:01.333
Trapped like that, the electrons can't 
interact with light...

00:09:01.625 --> 00:09:03.125
and so it just passes through.

00:09:04.375 --> 00:09:06.250
We've reached the center of the earth...

00:09:06.666 --> 00:09:09.416
but that's not the end because 
we can continue into pressures

00:09:09.416 --> 00:09:11.541
found inside larger plants.

00:09:12.666 --> 00:09:15.833
Tens of thousands of kilometers
below Jupiter's surface...

00:09:16.166 --> 00:09:19.125
Physicists think hydrogen will go through 
another change

00:09:19.125 --> 00:09:21.750
becoming a shiny conductor of electricity.

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:23.583
It's thought that a lot of Jupiter

00:09:23.583 --> 00:09:25.791
is made up of this metallic hydrogen.

00:09:26.416 --> 00:09:29.583
We think of high energy 
density materials

00:09:29.583 --> 00:09:32.166
as completely inverting 
the periodic table

00:09:32.166 --> 00:09:34.250
so your metals become transparent

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:36.500
and your transparent materials 
become metals...

00:09:36.875 --> 00:09:39.500
and all these gases become solids...

00:09:39.958 --> 00:09:42.125
And the universe holds 
higher pressures still.

00:09:42.458 --> 00:09:45.833
The center of Jupiter sees over 
10 million atmospheres

00:09:45.833 --> 00:09:48.875
just about the highest pressure
that the Omega laser can create.

00:09:49.708 --> 00:09:51.875
And now we're diving into the sun...

00:09:52.291 --> 00:09:55.708
where pressures rise over 
100 billion atmospheres.

00:09:56.458 --> 00:09:58.958
The island of Manhattan balanced on a phone.

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:02.708
We've seen extreme pressures, 
overwhelming the forces

00:10:02.708 --> 00:10:04.083
that keep molecules apart.

00:10:04.541 --> 00:10:07.000
But here within the sun, 
they can overcome

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:09.583
the very glue that holds atoms together.

00:10:10.083 --> 00:10:14.000
Here, individual hydrogen nuclei 
can be used to form helium...

00:10:14.416 --> 00:10:16.375
a process that releases energy.

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:19.458
This is nuclear fusion:

00:10:19.458 --> 00:10:21.750
The ultimate source of all energy 
in our solar system.

00:10:22.083 --> 00:10:25.250
The reaction at the center 
of every twinkling star.

00:10:25.916 --> 00:10:26.625
If we could somehow

00:10:26.625 --> 00:10:29.125
recreate this process on Earth 
and keep it going...

00:10:29.583 --> 00:10:33.083
we would have a near limitless source 
of clean, cheap power.

00:10:33.625 --> 00:10:34.916
And researchers around
the world

00:10:34.916 --> 00:10:37.333
are using giant lasers, 
including Omega...

00:10:37.541 --> 00:10:39.125
to study this possibility.

00:10:41.875 --> 00:10:45.000
This is all a relatively new frontier 
of physics.

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:47.750
Scientists still have so many questions 
about the rules

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:49.958
about how different elements and substances

00:10:49.958 --> 00:10:52.166
act and interact under different conditions...

00:10:52.416 --> 00:10:54.916
and how that might influence 
the evolution of planets...

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:57.208
and their ability to foster life.

00:10:57.791 --> 00:10:59.750
They'll keep chipping away at those unknowns...

00:11:00.041 --> 00:11:02.666
one split second experiment at a time.

00:11:05.083 --> 00:11:07.291
[Lump of Coal by Adam Cole]
Hold me close...

00:11:07.291 --> 00:11:09.541
Squeeze me tight...

00:11:09.541 --> 00:11:12.125
Get together/
Up the pressure

00:11:12.125 --> 00:11:14.666
Feels so wrong/
but it feels so right...

00:11:16.041 --> 00:11:19.583
Break me down/
Then you make me whole...

00:11:19.583 --> 00:11:22.458
You want a diamond/
take your time and

00:11:22.458 --> 00:11:25.958
keep on tryin/
‘cause I’m just another coal.

00:11:27.875 --> 00:11:30.666
I’m just another coal!

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:35.166
[Lump of Coal by Adam Cole fades]

